// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6436 Add Linux rule: Potential Command Execution Via Tcpdump Postrotate Command
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6436
// Pull request author: defamp
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Command Execution Via Tcpdump Postrotate Command
// Sigma ID: 8eba4cc7-4ffc-4e5b-9e2f-6b9ef43cf225
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Defa Mulya Pratama
// Date: 2026-10-07 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects execution of "tcpdump" with the "-z" (postrotate) option pointing to a shell, a script
//   located in a temporary directory, or combined with "-Z root". The "-z" option runs the specified
//   command after every rotated capture file. When "tcpdump" is executed with elevated privileges
//   (e.g. via "sudo"), this is abused to execute arbitrary commands as root, a well-known Linux
//   privilege-escalation primitive.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the "-z" option to run a compression utility (e.g. "gzip") on rotated capture files will generally not match, as it lacks the suspicious indicators required by this rule.
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/tcpdump/
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/linux-restricted-shell-breakout-via-linux-binary-s.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/288411871885b23566931b880232c0b65b93906b/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_tcpdump_postrotate_command.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/tcpdump" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -z " and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/tmp/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/dev/shm/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/var/tmp/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -Z root")
